PokeDaisy's reference data (the kiwami fork of BananaOS)

The files in this folder hold what PokeDaisy knows about every mainline Pokémon game it supports, English releases
only: the RAM addresses and layouts its readers read, where the ROM's tables are, its guides' bosses and areas by ids
and flags, and its own words (its guide pages, its item descriptions). They are extracted from PokeDaisy by the fork's
kiwami/tools/pokedaisy-extract.py (--reference); README.md lists what each file holds and what was left out, and
SOURCES names the commit read and the SHA-256 of every file read and written. They are reference data: nothing here is
installed in the image or read by banana-ui. Nothing of the games themselves (their names, text, pictures or tables)
is here, but for the place and boss names a guide names its bosses by and what PokeDaisy's own words name.

